---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on SingaporeSalary.com: None at All" description="SingaporeSalary.com places no cookies and saves nothing on your device; Microsoft Clarity runs without cookies purely to spot errors in the CPF and tax tools." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Cookies', path: route('cookies', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Cookies</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>SingaporeSalary.com does not put any cookie in your browser, and neither does any service it loads. With nothing to agree to, the site shows no cookie notice.</p>
    <h2>The CPF and tax calculators</h2>
    <p>Your monthly wage, bonus, age and residency status stay in the open page. They are never saved to a cookie, to local storage or to session storage; once you change a field they are copied into the address bar, so the link itself can be shared, and they vanish with the tab otherwise.</p>
    <h2>Microsoft Clarity, cookieless</h2>
    <p>We keep a single technical script, Microsoft Clarity, to detect faults in the site. Before it loads, the page instructs it that storage is denied, so it stores none of its usual identifiers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>no <code>_clck</code> and no <code>_clsk</code> on this domain;</li>
      <li>no <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code> on Microsoft’s domains.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every page view is given a one-off identifier, so separate visits are not connected. What comes back to us is technical: JavaScript errors, how long pages take to load, clicks that lead nowhere and how far down a page people scroll. Page wording and anything typed into the CPF, bonus or relief fields is masked before it leaves your browser.</p>
    <p>Operator: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland. Retention: 30 days for recordings, 13 months for aggregates. Basis: our legitimate interest in calculators that work. To opt out, block <code>clarity.ms</code> or email us; CPF and take-home results are unaffected.</p>
    <h2>No analytics, no ads</h2>
    <p>The site runs no audience analytics and no advertising, and the publisher holds no personal data on its visitors. Questions: see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
